PARITY — every web branch reproduced (no scope narrowing)
  - 3 visuals in the web priority order: remote image (AsyncImage load/loaded/failed) ->
    deterministic 2-letter initials disc -> generic glyph (SF person.fill for `user`,
    a drawn Helix brand mark for `bot`).
  - djb2 seed hash -> colorIndex = djb2(seed) % 8 over the Okabe-Ito CB-safe palette.
    AvatarPalette.swatches is pinned == web CHART_COLORS_CB_SAFE == Color.TS.chartCategorical.
    Cross-impl parity pinned against the web reference (node djb2): "?"->2, "u-1"->4, "u-2"->7,
    "Ada Lovelace"->2, "Grace Hopper"->7, "John Doe"->0.
  - avatarInitials: 2 words -> first letters; 1 word -> first 2 chars; empty/whitespace -> "?".
  - isAttributed neutral-disc fallback for the anonymous (bot) case (web `--surface-2`).
  - presence dot online/idle/offline -> statusSuccess/statusWarning/textMuted + a11y label.
  - sizes xs16/sm24/md32/lg48, shapes circle/rounded, optional tooltip (`.help` + a11y).
  - States rendered (never blank): loading (fallback under a veil), loaded, failed->fallback,
    empty (neutral glyph disc), presence offline. The web primitive's only "offline" concept
    is the presence dot; reproduced faithfully (no fabricated QueryError/retry the source lacks).
  - i18n: avatar.unknown / avatar.statusOnline / avatar.statusIdle / avatar.statusOffline all
    resolve through the P1/S10 facade; zero English literals in the Swift sources.
  - P1/S8 state-holder seam (AvatarSource + AvatarModel), P1/S11 telemetry (view.opened
    surface="Avatar"), P1/S9 tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade — all present and consumed.
  - Accessibility: single VoiceOver element (label=identity, value=presence, .isImage trait),
    Dynamic Type initials (minimumScaleFactor), reduce-motion-gated image fade, luminance-derived
    foreground for WCAG contrast on every swatch (improvement over the web's fixed white).

